> But I'm not running in ascii mode...I just doubleclick the icon in
> windows...so I don't know how to pass the -u wizard -D argument to the
> app...

Right-click on nethackw.exe, "Create shortcut".
Right-click on the shortcut, "Properties", add the parameters to the
"target" section.

Then, double-click on nethackw.exe to get standard NetHack, double-click
on the new shortcut to get wizard mode NetHack.

